e first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x+3{)}^{2}-{3}^{2}+14\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x+3{)}^{2}+5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=3$ and $q=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141539/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "366b36a5-c909-5ea5-a05d-a6052fcd41d7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141539"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-250454/field-1/fa29778cd018d8ca462d8ec9f1dc4fa3adc5ff69fc9d917feeac71566157e013" :answer/id #uuid "0273277f-c26f-5856-9e22-6afc6e471f1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-250454/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "69e1c7e3-fca8-589e-9222-fded93cf61fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-250454/field-1/fa29778cd018d8ca462d8ec9f1dc4fa3adc5ff69fc9d917feeac71566157e013" :answer-field/choices ["q-250454/field-1/fa29778cd018d8ca462d8ec9f1dc4fa3adc5ff69fc9d917feeac71566157e013"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-250454/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "ed165bd7-7d94-5066-8699-206f7f41ffe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-250454/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "58e8a61d-0665-56f6-84ad-3ba919a1dad4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-250454/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-250454/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-250454" :question/id #uuid "543f6b63-b23f-5799-bcd2-45789ff9ae82" :question/math-academy-id "q-250454" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${y}^{2}+8y+13.$\n\n${y}^{2}+8y+13=(${{field-1}}${)}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+2\\cdot 4y+13\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${4}^{2},$ writing the constant term $13$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}+2\\cdot 4y+{4}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{4}^{2}+13\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y+4{)}^{2}-{4}^{2}+13\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y+4{)}^{2}-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-250454/field-1" "q-250454/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "366b36a5-c909-5ea5-a05d-a6052fcd41d7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-250454"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-3662/selection/9dc257bc74a9c1e9b7c13147aa8633a56bb8ebd95823b879ed3d65524163c694" :answer/id #uuid "a334d4f7-c953-51b7-8e6b-3e2b4128dce7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-2,\\text{ }q=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3662/selection/5019fecbd3e354066ee0d35e125576691e872204672fd49825c7e7f1eb6ad90a" :answer/id #uuid "1c9ec5c2-55c3-5cdc-9442-9ad1f20354c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-1,\\text{ }q=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3662/selection/281ada75a3623cf9849a7baece61d490807c761d8d2e748c146b246ad7c67200" :answer/id #uuid "70e5348c-b23e-5dbd-ad42-1e88a28c8080" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-1,\\text{ }q=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3662/selection/2c11fd13ac315b0973229cb62cbbf033a9f0cbcd8de848ec766c09c863cdc6d5" :answer/id #uuid "c961ba00-4415-51c2-a9fa-d5d503c8919a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-2,\\text{ }q=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3662/selection/3ac062b4833887f2a54839aec0704d471b8ca5f5620b8900ec5fd2340c7041ef" :answer/id #uuid "c7d22d74-b8e4-504c-8234-892dcb916479" :answer/type :