problem "If the expression ${y}^{2}-10y+30$ is written as $(y+p{)}^{2}+q,$ then what are the values of $p$ and $q?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+30\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${5}^{2},$ writing the constant term $30$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{5}^{2}+30\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y-5{)}^{2}-{5}^{2}+30\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y-5{)}^{2}+5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-5$ and $q=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141622/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c6d8d6-3d86-5074-bf99-0cb744c9412a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141622"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-250466/field-1/ebb95e1a4ce30d95a498ba3efbf7558fb3c5c1bc9219c3a2b06a2963d4938b5c" :answer/id #uuid "8c153580-0e8b-583a-adbd-a16b2852c4d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-250466/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6be369a-d0d7-5392-abd1-300ff2da78f1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-250466/field-1/ebb95e1a4ce30d95a498ba3efbf7558fb3c5c1bc9219c3a2b06a2963d4938b5c" :answer-field/choices ["q-250466/field-1/ebb95e1a4ce30d95a498ba3efbf7558fb3c5c1bc9219c3a2b06a2963d4938b5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-250466/field-2/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer/id #uuid "5a409531-6def-56bf-9660-d9e2ac26e842" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-250466/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e7b2932-b191-5cab-a360-12935f8165f3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-250466/field